  "title": "STM32MP135 DDR3 DQM Write Mask Failure (Byte writes only)",
  "content": "<p>I have a custom design with STM32mp135f + MT41K256M16TW-107 DDR3L @ 533MHz that I want to bring up. I built a Linux image based on OpenSTLinux guides and it boots until my kernel is loaded (uboot logs : “starting kernel”) then its crashes without any logs even with earlycon. By testing the DDR with ST DDR Tool, I realized that byte-masked writes fail (test 9), but halfword &amp; RMW32 work. <br /> </p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/ef5aa710-c6a2-4583-922a-affaffa2e7f0.png\" /></figure><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/adfc02c5-9927-4b4e-bc84-36bebfdd4c3b.png\" /></figure><p>I noticed the byte lane swap but it is identical on the dk board. I am a bit lost and don’t know if the issue is timing/config related or due to my hardware design. <br /> </p>",
